    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.comment\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nStandard (neo)vim textobjects work both in operator mode and in visual mode, unlike the mini.comment textobject.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.5\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nWith the following config:\r\n```\r\ncomment.setup {\r\n  mappings = {\r\n    comment = '<Space>c',\r\n    comment_visual = '<Space>c',\r\n    comment_line = '<Space>cc',\r\n    textobject = 'ic',\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n`dip` - deletes paragraph\r\n`dic` - deletes comment block\r\n`vip` - selects paragraph\r\n`vic` - does nothing\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n`vic` should select the comment block",
