        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@drybalka  In case you want the best of both words, this allows me **with the same keymap** to select textobject when visual selecion is empty, and comment visual selection otherwise\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nfunction is_visual_selection_empty()\r\n  -- works even without exiting visual mode\r\n  if vim.fn.mode() == 'V' then\r\n    -- VISUAL-LINE\r\n    return false\r\n  elseif vim.fn.mode() == 'v' then\r\n    -- VISUAL (char)\r\n    local start_pos = vim.fn.getpos('.')\r\n    local end_pos = vim.fn.getpos('v')\r\n    return vim.deep_equal(start_pos, end_pos)\r\n  else\r\n    return false\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- remap comment_visual for allowing textobject when empty selection\r\nvim.keymap.set(\r\n  \"x\",\r\n  \"gc\",\r\n  function()\r\n    if is_visual_selection_empty() then\r\n      return [[:<c-u>lua MiniComment.textobject()<CR>]]\r\n    else\r\n      return [[:<c-u>lua MiniComment.operator('visual')<cr>]]\r\n    end\r\n  end,\r\n  { desc = \"Comment selection\", expr = true }\r\n)\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2024-05-07T07:13:17Z",
